cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the associated data, please cite both this repository and the Zenodo data deposit."
title: "Behavioural video quantification for Gymnocypris eckloni under warming: code and annotations"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/CHAO-MA-Job/Gymnocypris-eckloni"
url: "https://github.com/CHAO-MA-Job/Gymnocypris-eckloni"
abstract: >-
  Code, image annotations and detector weights for a contact-free pipeline that quantifies
  fish behaviour from below-tank video. An eight-category ethogram decomposes swimming into
  opercular, pectoral and caudal regions; a stock YOLO11n detector labels these regions frame
  by frame, and post-processing converts the labels into continuous indices of locomotion and
  of organ-level action. Demonstrated on 15 Gymnocypris eckloni across 16-25 C.
keywords:
  - Gymnocypris eckloni
  - fish behaviour
  - thermal stress
  - object detection
  - YOLO11n
  - ethogram
  - non-invasive monitoring
